From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] save_prev_bl_data: export androidboot.revision

On Samsung sdm845 devices the board revision is known only to the primary
bootloader, which reads it from hardware, passes it as androidboot.revision
on the cmdline, and uses it to pick which starqlte-revNN.dtb to load.

When u-boot is chainloaded in place of the kernel that information is lost:
u-boot builds its own cmdline and nothing forwards the revision, so the OS
cannot tell a rev12 board from a rev14 one. That matters because the wifi
NVRAM is per-revision RF calibration -- PA coefficients, max TX power,
antenna gain, RSSI correction -- so shipping one variant to every unit
miscalibrates all the others, silently and without any error.

The previous bootloader's fdt is already located and validated here in
order to save prevbl_fdt_addr, so pull the revision out of its
/chosen/bootargs while we are looking at it and export it as
prevbl_revision. A boot script can then append it to the kernel cmdline.

This only sets an environment variable. If the fdt, the property, the key
or the value is missing, the variable is simply not set and boot is
unaffected.

Note for upstreaming: the revision is read where the /chosen node is
already resolved, which today sits behind SAVE_PREV_BL_INITRAMFS_START_ADDR.
Exporting the revision is logically independent of that option and the
lookup should be hoisted before sending this anywhere.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
---
--- a/arch/arm/lib/save_prev_bl_data.c
+++ b/arch/arm/lib/save_prev_bl_data.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/errno.h>
 #include <asm/system.h>
 #include <asm/armv8/mmu.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 
 static ulong reg0 __section(".data");
 
@@ -45,6 +46,40 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
+/**
+ * Export androidboot.revision from the previous bootloader's cmdline.
+ *
+ * The board revision is read from hardware by the primary bootloader and is
+ * not discoverable once it is gone, so forward it if it is there. Absence is
+ * not an error: not every primary bootloader sets it.
+ */
+static void save_prev_bl_revision(const void *fdt_blob, int node)
+{
+	static const char key[] = "androidboot.revision=";
+	const char *args, *val, *end;
+	char buf[16];
+	int len;
+
+	args = fdt_getprop(fdt_blob, node, "bootargs", &len);
+	if (!args || len <= 0)
+		return;
+
+	val = strstr(args, key);
+	if (!val)
+		return;
+	val += sizeof(key) - 1;
+
+	end = val;
+	while (*end && *end != ' ')
+		end++;
+	if (end == val || (size_t)(end - val) >= sizeof(buf))
+		return;
+
+	memcpy(buf, val, end - val);
+	buf[end - val] = '\0';
+	env_set("prevbl_revision", buf);
+}
+
 int save_prev_bl_data(void)
 {
 	struct fdt_header *fdt_blob;
@@ -71,6 +106,9 @@
 					__func__, reg0);
 		return -ENODATA;
 	}
+
+	save_prev_bl_revision(fdt_blob, node);
+
 	/*
 	 * linux,initrd-start property might be either 64 or 32 bit,
 	 * depending on primary bootloader implementation.
